{"id":57182,"ord":58,"n_segments":150,"prev":57181,"next":57183,"doc":{"id":"68190","title":"68190_Samuel","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Samuel Lovett","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68190/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68190"},"chapter":"Bennie Moten, Basie and the Reno","title":"Who played in Moten's band","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Goodwin names Jack Washington, Harlan Leonard, Woody Walder, Vernon Page and drummer Mack Washington as earlier members.","period":"1920s","year_from":1920,"year_to":1929,"words":156,"start":[81,6],"end":[83,0],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68190#s57182","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Bennie Moten's band","focus":1,"leader":"Bennie Moten"},{"name":"Walter Page's Blue Devils","focus":0,"leader":"Walter Page"},{"name":"Harlan Leonard's Rockets","focus":0,"leader":"Harlan Leonard"},{"name":"Thamon Hayes's band","focus":0,"leader":"Thamon Hayes"},{"name":"Count Basie Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Count Basie"}]},"people":[{"name":"Harlan Leonard","qid":"Q362528","n":3},{"name":"Count Basie","qid":"Q107008","n":2},{"name":"Mack Washington","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Woody Walder","qid":"Q30044303","n":2},{"name":"Vernon Page","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Jack Washington","qid":"Q6115675","n":2},{"name":"Benny Moten","qid":"Q672295","n":1},{"name":"Thamon Hayes","qid":"Q16008391","n":1},{"name":"Herman Walder","qid":"Q1610371","n":1},{"name":"Walter Page","qid":"Q1382200","n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":81,"b":6,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"Who were some of the other people joining the band, Crook, at that time?"},{"p":81,"b":7,"s":"MR. GOODWIN","x":"Jack Washington."},{"p":81,"b":8,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"Oh, the great Jack Washington, yes."},{"p":82,"b":0,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"Now he went with Basie --"},{"p":82,"b":1,"s":"MR. GOODWIN","x":"Played alto and baritone."},{"p":82,"b":2,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"Well, didn't he go with Basie?"},{"p":82,"b":3,"s":"MR. GOODWIN","x":"He went with Basie. Harlan Leonard."},{"p":82,"b":4,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"Oh the great Harlan Leonard."},{"p":82,"b":5,"s":"MR. GOODWIN","x":"Woody Walder, tenor man."},{"p":82,"b":6,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"Herman's brother."},{"p":82,"b":7,"s":"MR. GOODWIN","x":"Herman Walder's brother, and let me see -- Walter Page."},{"p":82,"b":8,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"On bass."},{"p":82,"b":9,"s":"MR. GOODWIN","x":"On bass."},{"p":82,"b":10,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"Was that before the Blue Devils?"},{"p":82,"b":11,"s":"MR. GOODWIN","x":"Not on the bass -- I'm ahead of myself. Vernon Keys was the bass player."},{"p":82,"b":12,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"Vernon Keys was the bass player, and Mack Washington was on drums?"},{"p":82,"b":13,"s":"MR. GOODWIN","x":"Mack Washington was on drums. Mack Washington was before any of the rest of them because I think he was with Benny when Benny had about six pieces. He was a kind of flashy drummer."},{"p":82,"b":14,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"Now this was before the Harlan Leonard band?"},{"p":82,"b":15,"s":"MR. GOODWIN","x":"Right."},{"p":82,"b":16,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"And the Thoman Hayes band?"},{"p":82,"b":17,"s":"MR. GOODWIN","x":"Right."},{"p":83,"b":0,"s":"MR. SMITH","x":"Right, all before that."}]}